@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how a published CLI release is resolved, verified and installed over the CDN
' covers: internal/cdn/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/update.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/update_test.go
' covers: apps/cli/public/cli/**
' covers: internal/cdn/stage/main.go
' covers: internal/cdn/stage/main_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/cli_tasks_test.go
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: .goreleaser.yaml
'
' ── MAINTAINER RELEASE PATH: mise tasks + goreleaser (2026-11-12) ──────────
' mise.toml owns the path; the one Go program on it is internal/cdn/stage.
'   snapshot ...... goreleaser release --snapshot --clean into dist/
'                   (version X-SNAPSHOT-<sha>)
'   release ....... depends release-ledger (a tagged HEAD and the retirement
'                   ledger, _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml), then goreleaser
'                   release --clean --skip=publish, then stage-cdn
'   stage-cdn ..... hidden; go run ./internal/cdn/stage
'   deploy-cli .... depends release, asks to confirm, then pnpm exec wrangler
'                   deploy --cwd apps/cli; scripted: `mise run --yes deploy-cli`
'   dev-cli ....... snapshot, stage-cdn, then pnpm exec wrangler dev; it
'                   never deploys
'   test-images ... snapshot and stage-cdn first, then the installer suite
'                   against that tree (PROVEO_INSTALLTEST_CDN)
'   build-cli ..... go install proveo and proveo-entrypoint into GOPATH/bin
'                   (env GOBIN = false; a `go env -w GOBIN` entry still
'                   wins), version dev@<sha> from build info
' goreleaser 2.17.0 is pinned on snapshot and release alone, never in [tools],
' so fmt, lint and post-commit never resolve it. goreleaser lists its binaries
' explicitly, and no maintainer program is among them.
' * stage reads the platforms from .goreleaser.yaml builds[id=proveo], the
'   version from dist/metadata.json, and the cdn-proveo Binary entries from
'   dist/artifacts.json. It checks each binary's sha256 against goreleaser's
'   extra.Checksum BEFORE it touches the tree, so a refused stage leaves bin/,
'   checksums.txt and latest.json as they were. Then it removes stale
'   bin/proveo-* files, copies each binary 0755, and writes checksums.txt and
'   latest.json (json.MarshalIndent of cdn.Manifest).
' * latest.json's version is goreleaser's, equal to the binaries' --version.
'   MEASURED 2026-11-12: latest.json, dist/metadata.json and
'   bin/proveo-darwin-arm64 --version all read 0.1.6-SNAPSHOT-7a0c8cf4, and
'   `shasum -a 256 -c checksums.txt` passed 8 of 8.
' * GONE on 2026-11-12 with the old stager: the cross-compile fallback, the
'   tar.gz/zip/flat/raw extraction, the legacy-asset reset, the git-describe
'   version chain, PROVEO_CDN_ROOT, PROVEO_DIST_DIR, PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST
'   and PROVEO_VERSION's stamp role. A dist/ missing a platform, its metadata
'   or a matching checksum now fails, naming `mise run snapshot` (or `mise run
'   release` on a tag).
' * Pinned by internal/cdn/stage/main_test.go and
'   internal/contract/cli_tasks_test.go (TestBuildCLIInstallsOnlyTheShippedBinaries,
'   TestGoreleaserIsPinnedPerTask, TestDeployCLIShipsOnlyATaggedRelease,
'   TestCDNStagingFollowsAFreshSnapshot).
' * .goreleaser.yaml emits the multi-arch static binaries AND a sha256
'   checksums.txt, so the installer can verify what it downloads. It replaced an
'   unverified `curl | bash` pipeline (moved from its header, N14).
' covers: internal/installtest/**
' covers: internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go
'
' ── ONE CHANNEL URL (N28, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ────────────────────────────
' install.sh reads ${PROVEO_ASSET_BASE_URL:-https://proveo.ca/cli} for the
' channel manifest, binary, checksums, and uninstall.sh. `proveo update` uses
' the same URL. The PROVEO_CLI_BASE_URL alias shipped in v0.2.0 and was removed
' before the next release; install.ps1 never read it. internal/installtest
' checks that a retired channel variable cannot override the configured URL.
' Open: PROVEO_VERSION only relabels an install (N34), and the installers spell
' PROVEO_SKIP_INIT and PROVEO_UNINSTALL_ASSUME_YES their own way (N36).
'
' ── THE INSTALL SUITE RUNS THE INTERPRETER USERS GET ───────────────────────
' internal/installtest executes the real install.sh / uninstall.sh. On darwin
' it invokes /bin/bash explicitly: the scripts' `#!/usr/bin/env bash` resolves
' to a Homebrew bash 5 on a maintainer Mac, which hides every 3.2 breaker that
' `curl … | bash` meets on a stock Mac. Elsewhere it takes bash from PATH.
'
' It stages its own CDN (go build ./cmd/proveo + checksums.txt + latest.json)
' so it stays hermetic and runs in the default test lane. PROVEO_INSTALLTEST_CDN
' points it at an already staged tree instead, to verify the release stage.
'
' The bootstrap cases serve a STUB proveo that records its argv. install.sh
' runs `proveo init` after placing the binary, and the real one reaches GitHub
' and installs sbx: a hundred-megabyte download inside a unit suite, on
' whatever host runs it.
'
' Inherited PROVEO_* variables are dropped from every child: a PROVEO_VERSION
' or PROVEO_SKIP_INIT in the operator's shell would otherwise steer the cases.
' internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go guards the same scripts statically
' (`/bin/bash -n`, bash-4-only syntax, unguarded "${arr[@]}" under set -u).
'
' ── THE INSTALLER PUTS PROVEO ON PATH (R4, 2026-11-11, FOUND 1, MEASURED) ──
' install.sh ran `PATH="$BIN_DIR:$PATH" proveo setup`, so setup found the dir
' on PATH, wrote nothing and exited 0, and install.sh skipped its own markers:
' a fresh install left no rc line (since 911280ea). It now runs
' `"$BIN_DIR/proveo" setup` with BIN_DIR left out of PATH
' (path_without_bin_dir), and setup matches the rc against this bin dir, not a
' marker alone (setup-path.puml, FOUND 9). The operator chose "fix install.sh
' + setup". With this shell's PATH, a dir there only by the hand `export` the
' closing text suggests read "already on PATH" and got no line: every CDN
' install that ran install.sh again (the R4 review, upkeep must-fix 7). A dir
' on PATH from a file setup does not read (~/.zprofile) now gets setup's
' line too: a repeated PATH entry, where the old call left new shells without
' proveo. NOT CHOSEN: change setup alone; leave it to the installer's owner;
' this shell's PATH (the hand case above). R3's deferred installer lines rode
' along: no `proveo init --print` suggestion right after init; init_incomplete
' says "proveo itself is installed; the sbx backend is not set up yet" and no longer
' "the lines above say which condition failed" after a quit; the closing text
' wrote "source \~/.zshrc" under /bin/bash 3.2 (`${x/#$HOME/\~}` keeps the
' backslash there, MEASURED) and now cuts the $HOME prefix with a case.
' internal/installtest pins it on the REAL-binary install (the stub CDN's
' proveo answers setup with exit 0): the rc holds setup's block once, still
' once after a second install, once when the bin dir is already on PATH, no
' install.sh marker, and the closing text holds "source ~/<rc>", no `\~`, no
' "init --print".
'
' ── WHAT `proveo update` PRINTS (R4 of _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml)
' No heading; one closing line, last; every × is the command's own item,
' Reported (exit 1, main prints nothing):
'   --check, newer   ● proveo 0.3.1 → 0.4.0 — available, the channel URL dim
'                    (Cloudf: the operator asked and nothing is wrong, P8)
'   current          ✓ proveo 0.4.0 — up to date (one wording, --check or not)
'   updated          ✓ proveo 0.3.1 → 0.4.0 — updated, dim ~/.proveo/bin/proveo
'                    (--force on the same release: "proveo 0.4.0 — reinstalled")
'   uninstall.sh     ⚠ ~/.proveo/uninstall.sh — not refreshed, error dim, above ✓
'   a local build    × proveo dev@<sha> — a local build, not replaced, dim
'                    "`proveo update --force` replaces it with 0.4.0"
'   latest.json      × latest.json — not read (it never arrived) or — not valid
'                    (it held no release), the cause dim without cdn's prefix;
'                    × latest.json — no checksum for <asset>
'   the download     × proveo 0.4.0 — not downloaded, cause dim without
'                    "download <asset>: "; × <asset> 0.4.0 — checksum mismatch,
'                    dim "expected <sum>" and "got      <sum>" (critique b1:
'                    the asset is what a report needs)
'   the replace      × ~/.proveo/bin/proveo — not replaced, error dim
' Three waits have a live line that leaves the screen: "latest.json —
' reading", "proveo 0.4.0 — downloading", "uninstall.sh — downloading" (each
' up to 60-120 s, critique must-fix 10). Plain output keeps the download's
' start line alone. cdn types its errors for this: ManifestError{Fetch},
' DownloadError, ChecksumMismatch; each Error() keeps a full sentence.
' updateAt takes the binary's path; doUpdate alone asks os.Executable, so a
' test never replaces its own binary (update_test.go serves a local channel).
' KNOWN, NOT FIXED: --check fails at ChecksumFor for a platform latest.json
' lacks before it checks (d5); a binary the operator cannot write (installed
' by root) fails with no how-to; `curl … uninstall.sh | bash` runs
' `proveo uninstall --yes` whenever stdin is not a terminal, so it asks
' nothing (uninstall.sh:13-14, critique d7).

title Distribution + self-update — install.sh and `proveo update`

actor "Consumer" as USER

node "Maintainer host" as MH <<host>> {
  component "goreleaser\nmulti-arch static binaries" as GR <<app>>
  component "mise run stage-cdn\ninternal/cdn/stage → apps/cli/public/cli" as STAGE <<app>>
}

cloud "Cloudflare — proveo.ca/cli" as CDN <<cloud>> {
  artifact "latest.json\n{version, checksums{basename→sha256}, base_url}" as MANIFEST <<db>>
  artifact "proveo-<goos>-<goarch>[.exe]" as ASSET <<db>>
}

node "Consumer host" as CH <<host>> {
  component "dist/install.sh · install.ps1" as INSTALL <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo update\n--check | --force" as UPD <<app>>
  component "internal/cdn\nBaseURL · FetchManifest\nCurrentAssetName · Newer\nDownloadAsset · IsDevVersion" as CDNPKG <<app>>
  component "proveo binary on PATH" as BIN <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo setup\nPATH via internal/shell" as SETUP <<app>>
}

GR ARROW_MAIN STAGE
STAGE ARROW_CLOUD CDN : wrangler deploy
USER ARROW_MAIN INSTALL
INSTALL ARROW_CLOUD MANIFEST : fetch
INSTALL ARROW_CLOUD ASSET : download
INSTALL ARROW_MAIN BIN : install + successLabel(sha256 verified)
INSTALL ARROW_MAIN SETUP : hand off PATH wiring\n(PATH without BIN_DIR)

USER ARROW_MAIN UPD
UPD ARROW_MAIN CDNPKG
CDNPKG ARROW_CLOUD MANIFEST : " ""FetchManifest(client, BaseURL())"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_MAIN CDNPKG : " ""Newer(remote, local)"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_CLOUD ASSET : " ""DownloadAsset(…, wantHex)"" "
CDNPKG ARROW_ERROR BIN : errorLabel(checksum mismatch → abort)
CDNPKG ARROW_MAIN BIN : atomic replace

note right of CDNPKG
  **Checksum is the trust root.** The asset is only
  installed when its sha256 matches the ""checksums""
  entry in ""latest.json""; a mismatch aborts without
  touching the installed binary. The manifest may
  redirect downloads via its own ""base_url"".

  ""AssetName(goos, goarch)"" is the naming contract
  shared by goreleaser, the staged CDN tree and the
  updater — they must agree or every update 404s.

  A dev build (""IsDevVersion"", e.g. ""dev@<sha>"") is
  never auto-replaced unless ""--force"" is passed, so a
  locally built binary is not clobbered by a release.
end note

note bottom of CDN
  Release assets only — no application code runs here.
  Publishing: an exact git tag builds semver artifacts
  (no GitHub Release); otherwise ""--snapshot"".
end note
note bottom of MANIFEST
  **One published channel, so a pinned version is not a time machine.** The
  installers read the version from ""latest\.json"" unless ""PROVEO_VERSION"" is
  set, and the bucket carries the current release only. MEASURED 2026-10-18: an
  explicit value only RELABELS — install.sh still downloads ""bin/$ASSET_NAME""
  (:307), so ""PROVEO_VERSION=0.1.1"" installs the latest binary and prints
  v0.1.1. This note used to say an older tag "resolves to nothing" (N34).
end note

@enduml
